{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WyFAiKaRwJUBFVe7tFpMkE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"attempt_id\": \"attempt-20260812T195323.560221Z-db704d6e1f\",\n3\t  \"branch_id\": \"ea9e364f6011f609d8b884cb8923d5eb79f9ae4b8a092dd5409acc4a9319cc8b\",\n4\t  \"commands\": [\n5\t    {\n6\t      \"argv\": [\n7\t        \"claude\",\n8\t        \"--print\",\n9\t        \"--model\",\n10\t        \"sonnet\",\n11\t        \"--effort\",\n12\t        \"high\",\n13\t        \"--permission-mode\",\n14\t        \"acceptEdits\",\n15\t        \"--allowedTools\",\n16\t        \"Read Edit Write Glob Grep Bash(/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest *)\",\n17\t        \"--output-format\",\n18\t        \"stream-json\",\n19\t        \"--verbose\",\n20\t        \"--no-session-persistence\",\n21\t        \"You are executing one node of the Plan 26 implementation prompt graph.\\nThe production curriculum factory MUST continue to use LangGraph exactly as specified.\\nDo not implement a Python replacement for that production runtime.\\nRun every pytest command as /tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest ...; never use python3, python, or plain pytest.\\nNode: N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\\nPatch provenance: {\\\"active_patch_ids\\\": [\\\"P-N31-001\\\"], \\\"base_prompt_sha256\\\": \\\"c540087d0e59c03f924ed65efecd23f18bd7079ec692486f010dd6464fb835a1\\\", \\\"effective_prompt_sha256\\\": \\\"5721bff7e17692b92bab4d4802929991421b585d6b91d321400b113e40dd6603\\\", \\\"patch_chain_sha256\\\": \\\"65a918ec93524292d7d3637107821d39bfb59acd2765b009a637a7484d2b16b6\\\", \\\"patch_ids\\\": [\\\"P-N31-001\\\"]}\\nDeclared writable paths: [\\\"runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py\\\", \\\"runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py\\\", \\\"runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py\\\", \\\"tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py\\\", \\\"plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md\\\", \\\"plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE\\\"]\\nCompact predecessor state: {\\\"N30_UNIT_GRAPH\\\": {\\\"outputs\\\": {\\\"plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/N30_UNIT_GRAPH.result.v1.md\\\": \\\"f04fbfcb10b95b3b0f86de7c88939c607f45c6cd60d1ee2d4ecf0df17db63ac3\\\", \\\"plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH\\\": \\\"c468b85043c905358dac9988a08f9bd95b51ae303426722a8a7d67559e857107\\\", \\\"runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py\\\": \\\"eae00c21bfe55ce6e2d6c4374611db4d84d286218d498fa520e799288e152e26\\\", \\\"runtime/langgraph_factory/unit_graph.py\\\": \\\"286995f398826be63bc2263ea5148f87b23ee7683973e4245c4ee3687a6f309c\\\", \\\"tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py\\\": \\\"914f6456429c81879bdaf0cacf54ba6b3e43b57f0fee2795ccfe0caf02e71d96\\\"}, \\\"receipt\\\": \\\"plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/v3/N30_UNIT_GRAPH.receipt.v1.json\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASSED\\\"}}\\nDo not read historical result Markdown or old evidence unless the node prompt names a specific file needed to diagnose a failure.\\nComplete the node's own TEST/LOOP before returning. The controller independently verifies the focused test command.\\n\\n--- BEGIN NODE PROMPT (verbatim) ---\\n# GOAL\\n\\nImplement `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE` after N30. Integrate D17\\u2013D24 and M06 into the\\nsame compiled graph for finding classification, targeted repair, invalidation/\\nretest, bounded convergence, immutable unit acceptance, checkpoint correlation,\\ncoverage, and routing of terminal candidates through the already implemented,\\nN22-owned D98.\\n\\nN31 owns repair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py. Every finding maps once;\\nattempts reserve before dispatch; repairs are versioned bounded children; D22\\nrecomputes the full current unit denominator. Unit success/failure tests invoke\\nthe real predecessor-provided D98 callable and never patch or replace it.\\n\\n# TEST\\n\\n1. Zero/multiple/unknown/model-selected finding owners fail.\\n2. Local repair changes only named paths/descendants; broad/in-place/stale repair fails.\\n3. Attempt/repeat bounds stop before an over-bound M06 call.\\n4. All invalidated descendants retest; stale evidence cannot pass.\\n5. Removing/failing/staling each acceptance member makes D22 reject.\\n6. Accepted bytes remain immutable across resume, later units, and repair.\\n7. Cursor advances only after checkpoint/evidence/log correlation flush.\\n8. D24 rejects missing/extra/reordered/wrong-hash coverage.\\n9. One-mode success and unit failure candidates traverse the real N22-owned D98;\\n   invalid terminal candidates are rejected, with no N31 write to terminal.py.\\n10. Crash at every repair/accept/checkpoint/D98 boundary is recoverable.\\n\\nWrite `results/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE.result.v1.md` with owner/retest maps,\\ndenominator and real-D98 traces, commands, and hashes.\\n\\n# LOOP\\n\\nPatch one classifier, repair, admission, retest, acceptance, coverage, or fixture\\nowner. Route any D98 defect back to N22; do not write terminal code here. Never\\nwiden repair or weaken a denominator.\\n\\n\\n\\n--- BEGIN APPROVED IMMUTABLE PATCH OVERLAY ---\\nPatch ID: P-N31-001\\nReason: N90's audit (finding F1) found D16-D23 fully implemented but never wired into the one production compiled graph, because N31's own module docstring deferred registration to N32 while N32's prompt deferred it right back. graph.py is now in N31's write set to close this ownership gap directly\\nExpected effect: D16-D23 become real, wired members of the compiled production graph; the six N31-owned DEFERRED_EDGES rows resolve; a real compiled fake-transport run reaches UNIT_ACCEPTED; binding_inventory()'s return value stays unchanged so N30's frozen tests keep passing\\nInstructions:\\nOwnership correction from N90's independent audit (finding F1). N90 found that\\nD16-D23 (the unit repair/acceptance cycle you implement) are fully implemented\\nand function-level tested, but never registered or wired into the one\\nproduction compiled graph (`build_curriculum_factory_graph()` in\\n`runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`). A real run can never reach\\n`D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED` for any unit \\u2014 only the isolated function\\ncalls your own tests exercise prove anything.\\n\\nRoot cause: your own `repair.py` module docstring says \\\"that registration is\\nN32's write\\\" \\u2014 deferring wiring to N32, who deferred it right back (N32's own\\nprompt says the workbook engine is \\\"not called by `build_curriculum_factory_\\ngraph`... N32 owns wiring this function into whatever the production compile\\npoint becomes once the workbook branch is in scope\\\"). Nobody wired D16-D23.\\n`graph.py` is now in your write set specifically to close this. Wire it here,\\nas the node that owns the repair/acceptance node bodies and is best placed to\\nprove them reachable.\\n\\n## What \\\"wired\\\" means and how the existing machinery already does most of it\\n\\nRead `runtime/langgraph_factory/unit_graph.py` in full before changing\\nanything \\u2014 do not re-derive its logic from memory. `unit_graph.register_\\nunit_path(builder, available)` already computes, for every `UNIT_BRANCHES`\\nsource (including D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN, D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT, D12_VISUAL_\\nBARRIER_AND_JOIN, D14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES, D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_\\nFAILURE, and M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT), which of their declared guard\\ndestinations currently have a registered node body (`branch_destinations`,\\nintersecting `MODEL_BRANCH_DESTINATIONS`/`routing.guard_destinations` against\\nwhatever `available` sequence is passed in) versus which stay deferred\\n(`deferred_destinations`, checked against the frozen `DEFERRED_EDGES` table).\\nThis means: once D16-D23's node bodies are present in the `bindings`/\\n`available` sequence that reaches `register_unit_path`, the six DEFERRED_EDGES\\nrows your work owns \\u2014\\n  (D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN, domain_repairable) -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS\\n  (D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT, content_repairable) -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS\\n  (D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN, visuals_repairable) -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS\\n  (D14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES, layout_repairable) -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS\\n  (D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE, repair) -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS\\n  (M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT, review_returned) -> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE\\nget wired automatically the next time `register_skeleton`/`register_unit_path`\\nruns with that widened set. You do not need to (and must not) edit\\n`unit_graph.py` itself \\u2014 it is N30's frozen write, already correct, and\\nalready designed for exactly this widening.\\n\\nWhat does not exist yet and is yours to add: (1) getting D16-D23's node\\nbodies into the bindings passed to `register_skeleton` at the one production\\ncompile point, and (2) the internal topology *within* D16-D23 itself \\u2014 the\\nloop spec section 8.2 describes (see the spec's own ASCII diagram, \\\"D16\\nPASS -> D22 -> D23 -> D05\\\", \\\"D16 FAIL -> D17 -> D18 -> D19 -> [deterministic\\nproducer, or D90 -> M06] -> D20 -> D21 -> earliest invalidated producer/check\\nin topological order -> D16\\\", \\\"D17/D29 repeat-bound or attempts-exhausted ->\\nD98\\\"). `UNIT_BRANCHES` in `unit_graph.py` does not declare D16-D23 as sources\\nat all \\u2014 that internal loop is not `unit_graph.py`'s concern, it is yours,\\nthe same way `workbook.register_workbook_path` is `workbook.py`'s concern for\\nD24-D32. Read `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py`'s `register_workbook_\\npath` and `graph.py`'s `register_workbook_topology` as the worked reference\\nfor this exact pattern (additive registration function, called once from the\\none production compile point, wiring a sub-cycle's internal edges over a\\nbuilder that already has the skeleton and unit path registered).\\n\\n## The one constraint that will break other nodes' frozen tests if you miss it\\n\\n`graph.py`'s `binding_inventory()` function has an explicit docstring warning:\\nseveral of N30's own tests in `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`\\nindependently recompute their expectations directly from `binding_inventory\\n()`'s *return value*. Do not change what `binding_inventory()` returns. N32\\nalready solved this exact problem for the workbook engine by introducing\\n`full_binding_inventory()` \\u2014 a separate, wider function (`binding_inventory()`\\nplus workbook bindings) used only at the compile point, leaving `binding_\\ninventory()` itself untouched for N30's tests to keep trusting. Follow the\\nsame pattern for D16-D23: either extend that composition one layer further,\\nor add your own comparably-named wider function, so `binding_inventory()`'s\\nreturn value is provably unchanged (assert this directly in your own test)\\nwhile `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` compiles against a set that includes\\nD16-D23. `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` is not in your write set\\nand is a required verification command for this node now specifically so a\\nregression here is caught before merge, not after.\\n\\n## Required proof (this is what makes the finding closed, not just \\\"code added\\\")\\n\\nYour own test file must independently prove, by executing the real compiled\\ngraph \\u2014 not by re-reading source or trusting N90's fingerprints are gone \\u2014\\nthat:\\n- D16-D23 are members of `build_curriculum_factory_graph(...).get_graph().\\n  nodes` (an actually compiled graph, the way N90's audit checked it:\\n  `compiled_topology()`/`compiled.get_graph().nodes`, not a declared table).\\n- Each of the six DEFERRED_EDGES rows you own is now a real, wired edge in\\n  that compiled graph, not merely absent from a \\\"still deferred\\\" set.\\n- A real run through the compiled production graph \\u2014 using the fake-CLI-\\n  transport/scripted-response pattern `tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.\\n  py` already established (see `_ScriptedFakeTransport`, `_HarnessContext`,\\n  and how N50 drives a real com