instruction to document this correction with full rigor): 6 tests in\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, 3 in\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`, and 1 in\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` now fail. Full\ndiagnosis, per-test root cause, and independent (Codex) confirmation that no\nalternative implementation avoids this are in \"P-N31-001 correction\" above.\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N32 and future generations)\n\n- The deterministic-vs-model routing table for `source interpretation` is\n  simplified to always route to M06 in this generation; spec section 12\n  allows a deterministic refetch when a locator remains authorized, which\n  would require a source-retrieval integration this node's write set does\n  not include (`repair.py`'s module docstring records the reasoning).\n- `compute_unit_denominator()`'s coverage of spec section 13.1 items 13-14\n  (append-log/evidence-index and checkpoint/state-digest integrity) is\n  structural, not a byte-level hash-chain re-audit from inside D22.\n- As of generation 2 (P-N31-001), D16-D23/M06 registration into the compiled\n  `StateGraph` is this node's write, not N32's — see \"P-N31-001 correction\"\n  above. N32 still owns D24-D32 and `workbook.py`/`register_workbook_topology`\n  entirely; this generation did not touch either.\n- `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, `test_plan26_topology.py`, and\n  `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` need a follow-up amendment (their\n  hardcoded narrow-`available`/exact-node-set fixtures, and the\n  `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER` receipt) to reflect that D16-D23 are now real,\n  production-wired graph members — see \"P-N31-001 correction\" above for the\n  specific tests and the reasoning; this node's write set does not include\n  any of those three files.","originalFile":"# N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE result\n\nstatus: PASSED (this node's own TEST 1-10 and the P-N31-001 required proof\nall pass; six pre-existing tests in the frozen `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`,\nplus downstream tests in `test_plan26_topology.py` and\n`test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py`, now fail as a structurally\nunavoidable consequence of closing N90 finding F1 — see \"P-N31-001\ncorrection\" below, which is the load-bearing section of this report)\nnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md\npredecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\ngeneration: 2 (generation 1 body unchanged below except where the P-N31-001\nsection says otherwise; generation 2 adds the graph.py wiring the patch\nrequires and documents its consequences)\n\n## What this node built\n\nTwo new top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns\nrepair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):\n\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18\n  (targeted repair planning), D19 (deterministic-vs-model routing), D20\n  (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch).\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator\n  reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +\n  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage\n  predicate N32 will call.\n\nAs of generation 2 (P-N31-001), both modules **are** registered into the one\nproduction compiled graph — see \"P-N31-001 correction\" below for the full\naccount. The rest of this section is generation 1's original description of\nthe node bodies themselves, which the patch did not change.\n\n`routing.py`'s guard tables for D16-D23 already exist (built by N20) and this\ngeneration's functions emit exactly the guard values those tables declare\n(`unit_denominator_passed`/`unit_findings_repairable`,\n`partition_complete`/`convergence_exhausted`, `repair_planned`,\n`model_repair`/`deterministic_repair`, `repair_admitted`,\n`retest_frontier_incomplete`/`retest_frontier_complete`, `unit_accepted`,\n`checkpoint_correlated`). Every function here is a plain, narrowly-scoped\n`(state, runtime_context) -> update` callable in the same shape N23's\n`model_nodes.py` already uses for D90/D91 — not wrapped in\n`nodes.deterministic_node()`, since that decorator requires a\n`NODE_CATALOGUE` row this generation is not permitted to add (`nodes/__init__.py`\nis not in N31's write set).\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls every function\ndirectly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged step-to-step\nthrough the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), not a mock merge —\nand, as of generation 2, also drives the real compiled production graph\nend to end (see below).\n\n## P-N31-001 correction (N90 finding F1)\n\n**What F1 said.** N90's independent audit found D16-D23 fully implemented\nand function-level tested by generation 1 of this node, but never registered\nor wired into the one production compiled graph\n(`build_curriculum_factory_graph()` in `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`).\nA real run could never reach `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED` for any unit —\nonly the isolated function calls generation 1's own tests exercised proved\nanything. Root cause: this module's own docstring deferred registration to\nN32, whose own prompt deferred it right back to \"whatever the production\ncompile point becomes once the workbook branch is in scope.\" Nobody wired\nD16-D23. P-N31-001 puts `graph.py` in N31's write set to close this directly.\n\n**What changed.** `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`:\n\n- `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` — a new function, `binding_inventory()`\n  (unchanged) plus `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` (D16-D23). Follows\n  the exact pattern N32 already established with `full_binding_inventory()`\n  for the workbook engine.\n- `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` now calls\n  `register_skeleton(builder, unit_repair_binding_inventory())` (previously\n  the narrow `binding_inventory()`), then calls\n  `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path(builder, sorted(bindings))`\n  afterward, over the same builder, to wire D16-D23/M06's own internal\n  sub-cycle edges (D17->D18->D19->[deterministic producer or D90->M06]->D20\n  ->D21->the owner's fixed retest chain, D16 PASS->D22->D23->D05).\n- `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` now maps D16-D23/M06 to `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE`\n  instead of leaving them as an undeclared gap.\n- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` gained\n  `register_unit_repair_path()` (the additive registration function,\n  directly analogous to `workbook.register_workbook_path`) and\n  `UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES`/`UNIT_REPAIR_TOPOLOGY_SOURCES`.\n- `unit_graph.py` was **not** touched, per the patch's instruction: widening\n  the `bindings`/`available` sequence that reaches\n  `unit_graph.register_unit_path` is what resolves the six\n  `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows this node owns — no edit to that frozen\n  module was needed or made.\n\nBecause `register_skeleton` now receives the widened bindings,\n`unit_graph.register_unit_path` (frozen, unedited) resolves the six\nN31-owned `DEFERRED_EDGES` rows automatically, exactly as the patch\npredicted. Verified directly against a real compiled graph (not a declared\ntable), in `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_topology_d16_d23.txt`:\n\n```\nD16-D23/M06 present in compiled().get_graph().nodes:\n  D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE: PRESENT\n  D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS: PRESENT\n  D18_PLAN_TARGETED_UNIT_REPAIR: PRESENT\n  D19_ROUTE_UNIT_REPAIR: PRESENT\n  D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR: PRESENT\n  D21_RETEST_REQUIRED_DESCENDANTS: PRESENT\n  D22_ACCEPT_UNIT: PRESENT\n  D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT: PRESENT\n  M06_REPAIR_NAMED_UNIT_ARTIFACT: PRESENT\n\nThe six N31-owned DEFERRED_EDGES rows, checked against the real compiled edge set:\n  (D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN, 'domain_repairable') -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS: REAL EDGE\n  (D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT, 'content_repairable') -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS: REAL EDGE\n  (D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN, 'visuals_repairable') -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS: REAL EDGE\n  (D14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES, 'layout_repairable') -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS: REAL EDGE\n  (D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE, 'repair') -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS: REAL EDGE\n  (M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT, 'review_returned') -> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE: REAL EDGE\n\nTotal compiled node count: 42\nbinding_inventory() count (must stay 32): 32\nunit_repair_binding_inventory() count: 40\n```\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` gained five new tests that\nindependently re-derive this same proof by executing the real compiled graph\n(not by re-reading source or trusting the fingerprints above are gone):\n`test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_real_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`,\n`test_binding_inventory_stays_unchanged_by_the_widened_production_compile`,\n`test_register_skeleton_accepts_the_widened_bindings_with_no_topology_error`,\n`test_a_real_compiled_graph_run_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`\n(the D16 PASS fast path: seeds a clean M05 review, `.invoke()`s the real\ncompiled graph, and D16/D22/D23/D05 all run for real, ending on the\nstill-deferred D24 row exactly as N32 will resolve it), and\n`test_a_real_compiled_graph_run_completes_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_back_to_d16`\n(a real D14->D17->D18->D19->D20->D21->D13->D14->D15->M05->D16 loop for a\ndeterministic-repair-owned `unit layout` finding, then acceptance — the D16\nFAIL path, not just the PASS one). All five pass; see\n`results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt`.\n\nFixed one real bug surfaced while building the second of those two tests:\n`compute_unit_denominator`'s page-inventory selection used\n`max(inventories, key=lambda record: record.get(\"page_count\", 0))`, which\npicks the *first* record on a page-count tie rather than the *current* one —\nwrong once a retest appends a same-page-count replacement inventory (exactly\nwhat a layout repair's retest does). `unit_page_inventories` is\n`append_unique`-reduced (append-only, in arrival order, the same convention\n`_latest_unit_review`'s `matches[-1]` and `visual_join[-1]` already use\nelsewhere in this same function), so the fix is `inventories[-1]`, matching\nthe file's own established \"current = last append\" convention throughout.\n\n**The regression this correction necessarily causes, and why it cannot be\navoided by a different implementation.** Wiring D16-D23 into the *same*\n`build_curriculum_factory_graph()` that `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py`,\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_topology.py`, and\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` also depend on\nnecessarily changes what those frozen files observe, because all of them\ncall that one function (or read a receipt keyed to `graph.py`'s hash) and\nnone of them are in this node's write set. Concretely:\n\n- `test_plan26_unit_graph.py::test_the_compiled_graph_registers_every_declared_unit_branch`\n  computes `expected = branch_destinations(source, available)` from\n  `available = tuple(sorted(G.binding_inventory()))` (deliberately narrow,\n  per the patch's own instruction not to change what `binding_inventory()`\n  returns), then asserts it equals `registered`, read from the *actual*\n  compiled graph's edges. Now that D08/D09/D12/D14/D91's guards really do\n  route to D17 (and M05's to D16) in that actual compiled graph, `registered`\n  correctly contains those destinations while `expected` — computed from the\n  frozen narrow set — does not. There is no way to make D08->D17 a real edge\n  in the one compiled graph this test also inspects while this exact\n  equality, computed from a deliberately-stale `available`, still holds; the\n  two requirements are logically exclusive over the same artifact.\n- `test_plan26_unit_graph.py::test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`,\n  `test_a_visual_denominator_permutation_produces_an_identical_admitted_head`,\n  `test_the_committed_path_stops_at_a_declared_deferred_edge`,\n  `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason`, and\n  `test_this_nodes_renderers_are_a_test_double_and_not_exposed_to_n13s_store_gap`\n  all run the shared single-unit `_build_episode_fixture` fixture through\n  `_run_episode`, whose scripted M05 review has no blocking findings. Before\n  this patch, that episode dead-ended at the `M05 -> D16` deferred edge\n  (D16 had no body), which several of these tests hard-code as\n  `deferred_frontier == \"D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE\"` or\n  `state[\"selected_unit_id\"] == \"U001\"` (true only because the episode never\n  got to call `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` a second time). Now that D16 really\n  executes, its denominator legitimately passes on the first try for this\n  clean fixture, so the real run proceeds through D22/D23, loops back to a\n  second `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` call, finds the one-unit manifest exhausted,\n  and correctly halts on the still-deferred `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`\n  row instead. This is the real pipeline behaving correctly — precisely the\n  behavior N90's finding said was missing — not a defect in this generation.\n- `test_plan26_topology.py` (N20's own frozen file, listing 3 failures) has\n  the same conflict one level up: `test_the_available_catalogue_compiles_against_real_node_callables`\n  and `test_the_builder_registers_a_fixed_node_set_independent_of_any_manifest`\n  both assert `set(compiled.get_graph().nodes) - {START, END} == set(binding_inventory())`\n  outright, which is now false by construction — the compiled graph has 42\n  nodes, `binding_inventory()` still has 32 (by design, per the patch).\n  `test_an_unwired_undeclared_node_fails_the_build_by_stable_id` fails for a\n  related reason: it pops one entry from `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` expecting the\n  build to reject it, but the entry it happens to pop (alphabetically first,\n  `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE`) is now genuinely wired rather than merely\n  declared-deferred, so removing its `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` row no longer\n  triggers `N20-NODE-UNDECLARED` — a case this frozen test's own fixture\n  logic cannot distinguish from the deferred case it was written to test.\n- `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py::test_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_after_harness_or_predecessor_change`\n  fails because `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER`'s receipt records a hash of\n  `graph.py` that this patch legitimately changed (the patch explicitly\n  authorizes N31 to edit `graph.py` as an ownership correction); the\n  controller's own receipt-staleness check correctly flags this, since it\n  cannot know from a hash alone that the edit was an approved correction\n  rather than an accidental collateral change. This is a receipt-bookkeeping\n  concern for the plan's controller layer, not a defect in `repair.py`,\n  `acceptance.py`, or `graph.py`'s own logic.\n\nI verified this diagnosis is not an artifact of a specific implementation\nchoice by independently confirming, with a second, isolated reviewer\n(a fresh Codex session given only the observed failures and asked to find\nany alternative that avoids them): no LangGraph mechanism, binding\ncomposition, or registration ordering reconciles \"D08->D17 is a real edge\nin `build_curriculum_factory_graph()`'s output\" with \"the frozen tests'\nhardcoded narrow-`available`/exact-node-set expectations, computed from\nthat same compiled artifact, still hold.\" (LangGraph's own\n`StateGraph.add_conditional_edges` keys `branches[source]` by the routing\nfunction's name and raises on a second registration under the same name for\nthe same source, which independently rules out a \"second, narrower branch\"\nworkaround, aside from the fact that `compiled_topology()`/`compiled.get_graph()`\nwould still show the real D08->D17 edge regardless of which LangGraph\nmechanism added it.)\n\n**Recommendation.** These three frozen test files were written before this\nownership correction existed, at a time when leaving D16-D23 unwired was the\n(mistaken, per F1) assumed final shape of this generation. `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`\nand `test_plan26_topology.py`'s specific hardcoded-narrow-`available`/\nexact-node-set assertions, and `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py`'s\nstale-receipt check for `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER`, need a follow-up amendment\n(updating `available`/expected-node-set fixtures to the widened set, and\nre-running/re-recording the `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER` receipt against the new\n`graph.py`) once this correction is accepted — not a contortion of this\nnode's own implementation to preserve assertions that assumed the finding\nthis patch exists to fix. No file outside this node's declared writable\npaths was edited to avoid or hide this consequence.\n\n## Owner / retest map\n\n| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |\n| curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |\n| unit content | content | model (M06) | `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT` |\n| unit visual | visuals | model (M06) unless every named key is an authoritative/library brief, then deterministic | `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS` |\n| unit layout | layout | deterministic (boundary-scoped pointer correction) | `D13_RENDER_UNIT` |\n\n`repair.RETEST_ORDER_BY_OWNER` carries each owner's full fixed chain (spec\nsection 12's table); D21 dispatches only the first node of that chain — the\nremaining steps are the already-wired unit-path edges (N30) that node's own\nsuccess guard reaches on its own, so D21 is never re-entered for the same\nrepair admission.\n\nFrozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17\nowns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns\nthe numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`). An earlier\ndraft of this generation checked both bounds in D17, which made\n`test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child` fail (D17 was\nexhausting a case the prompt's own TEST item expects D18 to exhaust) — fixed\nby removing the attempt-bound check from D17, per spec's own row split (\"D17\n... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt bound = exhaustion\").\n\n## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n\nRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\nminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\nCategories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),\ndomain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content\ncheck set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join\nresult, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\nindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\nthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\nverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\nunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\nindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\nconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\nconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\nreduction (stale evidence cannot pass) without needing to delete anything —\n`compute_unit_denominator` only counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the\n*current* head.\n\nDocumented, not silently assumed, scope limit: this generation's denominator\ntreats the append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer\nas structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\nthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\nsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this so\na future generation tightens it rather than rediscovering the gap.\n\n## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports\n`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` unmodified and calls\n`terminal.write_terminal()` directly — the identical function N22 wrote and\nN32 will call for its two product-terminal sites — never a stand-in:\n\n- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:\n  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from this generation's real D22/D23\n  output is independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own\n  `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n- `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the\n  same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes\n  `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own\n  re-derivation did.\n- `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`:\n  the `terminal_candidate` D18 proposes on attempt-bound exhaustion is\n  independently accepted by D98's `_validate_exhausted`.\n\nNo test in this file, and no code in `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, writes to\n`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\nstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n\n## Commands and results\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py -v\n=> 37 passed in 0.69s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -v\n=> 6 failed, 87 passed in 6.80s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/n30_unit_graph_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime -k plan26 -q\n=> 10 failed, 1056 passed, 1 skipped, 174 deselected, 345 subtests passed in 30.37s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n```\n\nThe 10 failures are exactly the ones documented and diagnosed in\n\"P-N31-001 correction\" above: 6 in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`, 3 in\n`test_plan26_topology.py`, 1 in `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py`.\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` (this node's own write set)\npasses 37/37, including the five new tests that independently prove the\npatch's required compiled-graph evidence. No other `plan26`-tagged test\nregressed: the pre-generation-1 baseline of 4 controller-test failures noted\nin generation 1 of this report is no longer present in this environment\n(the receipt state that caused those has since been refreshed by later\nnodes), and this run's 10 failures are a disjoint, newly-diagnosed set.\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python - <<'PY'\n# results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_topology_d16_d23.txt\n# builds the real compiled graph and checks D16-D23/M06 membership plus the\n# six N31-owned DEFERRED_EDGES rows against its actual node/edge set.\nPY\n=> all nine D16-D23/M06 nodes PRESENT; all six owned DEFERRED_EDGES rows\n   REAL EDGE; binding_inventory() count unchanged at 32; compiled node\n   count 42 (results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_topology_d16_d23.txt)\n```\n\n## Hashes\n\n| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` | `bea015578eec0d5167c7cafce79dec0bba2413b45fb150228886a4114cd59edf` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` | `fb20c76bf7d6eb2c0d216e3647cb52a8aa0597909c53bcc9eb68459ed4d74f63` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | `6ce29632586acd027a5e58e959a87049455618e19b666e941612fd3cd5f41716` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` | `5d87a82e152cf5af644c36d07176caa61e58a4431d5a34932e6c9755ad83cccc` |\n\n## TEST item verdicts\n\n1. **PASSED** — `test_d17_rejects_a_finding_with_no_owner`,\n   `test_d17_rejects_a_finding_with_an_unknown_owner`,\n   `test_d17_partitions_a_multi_owner_findings_list_into_separate_owner_entries`,\n   `test_review_finding_category_is_never_trusted_as_an_owner`.\n2. **PASSED** — `test_a_correctly_scoped_model_repair_admits`,\n   `test_a_broad_repair_outside_its_boundary_is_refused`,\n   `test_an_in_place_no_op_repair_is_refused`,\n   `test_a_stale_parent_repair_is_refused`,\n   `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_changes_only_its_allowed_pointer`.\n3. **PASSED** — `test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child`,\n   `test_fingerprint_repeat_bound_exhausts_at_d17`.\n4. **PASSED** — `test_d21_dispatches_the_first_retest_node_of_the_owners_fixed_chain`,\n   `test_stale_evidence_at_an_old_head_cannot_pass_the_denominator`.\n5. **PASSED** — `test_d22_accepts_a_fully_passing_denominator`,\n   `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject` (×5),\n   `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`.\n6. **PASSED** — `test_accept_once_refuses_a_differing_second_write_for_the_same_unit`,\n   `test_an_already_accepted_unit_can_never_re_enter_classification_or_planning`.\n7. **PASSED** — `test_d23_writes_checkpoint_metadata_and_cursor_in_the_same_update`,\n   `test_d23_refuses_to_advance_the_cursor_with_no_accepted_receipt`.\n8. **PASSED** — `test_coverage_proof_rejects_missing_extra_reordered_and_wrong_hash`.\n9. **PASSED** — `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`,\n   `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`,\n   `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`.\n10. **PASSED** — `test_repeating_d22_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_repeating_d23_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_re_admitting_the_same_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,\n    `test_a_crash_before_the_terminal_write_still_lets_d98_be_invoked_cleanly`.\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N32 and future generations)\n\n- The deterministic-vs-model routing table for `source interpretation` is\n  simplified to always route to M06 in this generation; spec section 12\n  allows a deterministic refetch when a locator remains authorized, which\n  would require a source-retrieval integration this node's write set does\n  not include (`repair.py`'s module docstring records the reasoning).\n- `compute_unit_denominator()`'s coverage of spec section 13.1 items 13-14\n  (append-log/evidence-index and checkpoint/state-digest integrity) is\n  structural, not a byte-level hash-chain re-audit from inside D22.\n- Registration of D16-D23 into the compiled `StateGraph` (`add_node`,\n  `add_conditional_edges`) is N32's write, per `implementation.graph.v3.yaml`\n  and `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md`; this generation does not add or edit\n  a line of `graph.py`, `unit_graph.py`, `routing.py`, or `nodes/__init__.py`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":387,"oldLines":6,"newStart":387,"newLines":36,"lines":["     `test_re_admitting_the_same_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,","     `test_a_crash_before_the_terminal_write_still_lets_d98_be_invoked_cleanly`."," ","+## P-N31-001 required-proof verdicts (generation 2 additions)","+","+11. **PASSED** — `test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_real_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`:","+    D16-D23/M06 are members of `build_curriculum_factory_graph(...).get_graph().nodes`.","+12. **PASSED** — same test: each of the six N31-owned `DEFERRED_EDGES` rows","+    is a real edge in `compiled_topology()`'s output, not merely absent from","+    a still-deferred set.","+13. **PASSED** — `test_a_real_compiled_graph_run_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`","+    (D16 PASS fast path) and","+    `test_a_real_compiled_graph_run_completes_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_back_to_d16`","+    (a full D17-D21 repair-and-retest loop back to D16): a real run through","+    the compiled production graph reaches `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/a real","+    `accepted_unit_receipts` entry for a unit, exercising both paths.","+14. **PASSED** — `test_register_skeleton_accepts_the_widened_bindings_with_no_topology_error`:","+    no `UnitTopologyError`/`GraphBindingError` is raised by `register_skeleton`","+    against the widened bindings.","+15. **PASSED** — `test_binding_inventory_stays_unchanged_by_the_widened_production_compile`:","+    `bind